---
/**
 * /wallpapers/faith — SEO landing page for the Faith / scripture category.
 * Chrome page (ChromeLayout), fully indexable, links through to the real
 * photos at /gallery#scripture.
 */
import ChromeLayout from '../../layouts/ChromeLayout.astro';
---

<ChromeLayout
  title="Christian & Faith Wallpapers for iPhone | motivationalwallpaper.com"
  description="Bible verse and scripture phone backgrounds"
>
  <h1>Christian & Faith Wallpapers for iPhone</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Scripture and steadying words, right where you'll actually see them.
  </p>

  <p>
    A lock screen is one of the most-seen surfaces on your phone — most
    people unlock it dozens of times a day, often without thinking. These
    faith wallpapers put scripture and short, steadying words in that same
    spot, so a moment that's usually reflexive becomes a small point of
    stillness instead. There's no need to remember to open an app or set a
    reminder; the verse is simply there, waiting, the next time you check
    the time or a notification.
  </p>
  <p>
    The category draws on deep navy and parchment tones with a quiet serif
    voice, built around a single steadying idea: be still, you are carried,
    you don't have to hold everything yourself today. It's meant for anyone
    who wants their faith to stay close during an ordinary Tuesday, not just
    during church on Sunday — a phone background that meets you in traffic,
    at your desk, or in a hard season, and reminds you who's holding it all
    together.
  </p>

  <p class="cta">
    <a href="/gallery#scripture">Browse the Faith wallpapers &rarr;</a>
  </p>
</ChromeLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--t-title1-size);
    font-weight: var(--t-title1-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--t-title1-track);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--t-lead-size);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }
  p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .cta {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .cta a {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
